---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Disclaimer — Stockbrowse" description="How to read Stockbrowse's scores and estimates, and what they are not.">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 text-[#94A3B8]">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-2">Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#64748B] mb-10">How to read what's on this site — and what it isn't.</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-slate-100 text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Not financial advice</h2>
        <p>
          Stockbrowse is for research and education. Nothing here is financial advice, an investment
          recommendation, or an offer to buy or sell any security. We don't know your situation, and the
          site doesn't account for it. Do your own research, and talk to a qualified advisor before you invest.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-slate-100 text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Scores describe, they don't predict</h2>
        <p>
          The Compass Score rates structural quality from public fundamentals. A high score means a company
          has looked financially healthy — it doesn't promise the stock will go up. Quality and price are
          different questions, and a great company can be a poor investment at the wrong price.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-slate-100 text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Fair Value is an estimate, not a target</h2>
        <p>
          The Fair Value range shows what a stock might be worth if it traded like its peers and its own
          history. It's descriptive, not a price target or a forecast of returns. Cheap can stay cheap, and a
          low estimate can be a value trap. The range needs decent analyst and fundamental coverage to mean much.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-slate-100 text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Catalyst and Golden are experimental</h2>
        <p>
          The Catalyst signal and Golden Stocks are based on historical patterns with a short live track
          record. We pre-registered the formula and track it forward in the open. Treat them as one input
          among many, not a buy signal. Past performance doesn't guarantee future results.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-slate-100 text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Data can be wrong or stale</h2>
        <p>
          Prices, fundamentals, and analyst figures come from third-party providers and can contain errors or
          lag the market. We refresh daily but make no guarantee of accuracy or timeliness. Verify anything you
          plan to act on against a primary source.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-slate-100 text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Affiliate links</h2>
        <p>
          Some links are affiliate links, and we may earn a commission if you open an account or make a
          purchase through them. That never affects our ratings — the scores are computed from data, not deals.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-xs text-[#64748B] pt-4 border-t border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.06)]">
        Questions? <a href="/how-it-works" class="text-[#22D3EE] hover:underline">See how the scores work</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
